    "title": "Wisconsin pickup truck driver strikes multiple trees after leaving roadway - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brianna Loving ,\n1 days ago PINE LAKE, Wis. (WFRV) – A pickup driver was not having the best of mornings after leaving the roadway and hitting several trees off of County Highway W on Tuesday morning.\nAccording to Pine Lake Fire Rescue , on August 4 around 7:00 a.m., firefighters were dispatched to a reported vehicle vs. tree accident on County Highway W near H&H Septic.\nCourtesy of Pine Lake Fire Rescue Upon arrival, crews noted a pickup truck that had left the roadway on a slight corner, resulting in striking multiple trees.\nThe driver, the only occupant, had exited the vehicle before prior to personnel respondence. The driver was seen by paramedics on scene, but declined transportation to any medical facility.\nWisconsin driver arrested for 5th OWI, drug and firearm possession: Reedsburg Police Firefighters assisted a wrecker company, cutting several of the stuck trees to remove the vehicle, on scene for one hour.\nNo other information was provided.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFRV Local 5 - Green Bay, Appleton.",
    "summary": "According to Pine Lake Fire Rescue , on August 4 around 7:00 a.m., firefighters were dispatched to a reported vehicle vs. tree accident on County Highway W near H&H Septic. Courtesy of Pine Lake Fire Rescue Upon arrival, crews noted a pickup truck that had left the roadway on a slight corner, resulting in striking multiple trees. The driver, the only occupant, had exited the vehicle before prior to personnel respondence.",
